   "summary": "<p>Three \\(n\\)-qubit registers holding signed integers \\(x, y, z\\), an angle \\(\\varphi\\), and a clean workspace. The goal is the operator that multiplies each basis ket by \\(\\exp(i\\pi\\varphi\\,xyz)\\) and does nothing else.</p><p>The statement is written without any circuit: <code>PTPPhaseOp</code> is a linear map the reader supplies, required only to act on every basis ket as <code>ptpEigenphase</code>. The theorem <code>ptp_lowerExact_correct</code> says a circuit built by the steps below equals it on every <em>clean</em> state. The rest of this diagram is how that circuit is built, one node at a time.</p>",
